1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
READING TASK

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,940
THE RETURN OF THE MILU DEER

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,360
I like to tell stories about people who work together.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,940
What is even better is when countries help each other and build a good friendship.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:27,380
An excellent example of this happened when Britain and China worked together to bring the Milu Deer back to China.

6
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,720
The Milu deer, a species with large horns(角),

7
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:38,560
used to be common in China long ago.Like other deer they lived together

8
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:43,100
and ate grass and the soft parts of trees such as small branches.

9
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:48,820
Milu deer were often hunted for food or sport in the past.

10
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:54,080
The Ming and Qing dynasties did not protect them and many were killed.

11
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:58,980
That is how the Milu deer disappeared from China.

12
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,540
Luckily before all of them were killed,

13
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:06,480
some were taken to Britain to improve the environment of the beautiful park

14
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,140
which belonged to the Duke of Bedford.

15
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:13,720
He liked them so much that he took them all the way from China to Britain.

16
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,180
The Milu deer liked the cool,

17
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:22,000
wet weather in England and their number increased year by year.

18
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,860
As a result, when in 1985 the government of China wanted to reintroduce the Milu deer,

19
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,100
the Duke of Bedford was happy to help.

20
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:50,960
The deer certainly seem happy to be back in China because their numbers have grown rapidly.

21
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,780
There are now so many of them that a new park has been opened

22
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,600
for them in Hubei Province.

23
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:03,240
At the moment the Milu deer live in centres where they are being well protected

24
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:04,360
and cared for.

25
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:09,740
It is hoped that one day there will be enough animals to let them live in the wild again.

26
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:15,960
So Britain helped China by bringing back an animal that had disappeared from its homeland.

27
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:22,080
This is a good example of friendship and understanding between these two countries.
